{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113853","id":3089910533,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc64LEsF","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113853","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113853.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113853.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113853","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113853/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113853/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113853/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ed2e2b21c074084b2e513ec7f3b6e61bf2a726c1","number":113853,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add option to skip subpass and tonemap directly on fragment on mobile renderer.","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds a feature to tonemap directly while drawing 3D geometry in the mobile renderer, a feature that might not be very useful for most projects as it affects the accuracy of the blending, but it can provide some extra performance for those projects that need it. This is the equivalent tonemapping process to the compatibility renderer, which also applies this adjustment directly when drawing.\r\n\r\nUsing this feature practically disables all other effects that can be applied during the tonemapping step, so it should only be used by projects that are fully aware of the consequences. On the mobile platforms this PR was tested on such as VR, it is estimated it can save around 0.5 to 1ms in total, which can be significant when targetting rates such as 90 Hz (~11 ms).\r\n\r\nAs a bonus, it also reorganizes the tonemapping code to share the implementations more effectively and it also adds support for specialization constants on Forward+'s tonemapper pass in the same way that the Mobile one does, which should provide it with some performance improvements.\r\n\r\nOpening up as draft to make it easier for me to self-review.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","c